            <ArticleTitle>Bariatric surgery: An HIV-positive patient's successful journey.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>70-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0956462415571971</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bariatric surgery is becoming increasingly common in the UK. Little has been done to evaluate its place in HIV-positive patients. Here, we discuss a successful case and the complexities surrounding highly active antiretroviral therapy.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© The Author(s) 2015.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
